# Cloudflare Pages redirect table for the published docs site.
#
# Read at the site root only, so this file has to carry the rules for every
# language tree. Without it a retired URL does not 404 -- Pages falls back to
# the site index and answers 200, which makes a dead link look alive to both
# readers and search engines.
#
# Two kinds of rule live here:
#
#   1. Renames. A page that moved keeps its old address working. Add a line
#      here in the same PR that renames the file, and add the /zh_CN/ twin.
#   2. Language-code guesses. The published Chinese tree is /zh_CN/ (the
#      gettext locale name); /zh and /zh-cn are what a reader actually types.
#
# Pages matches these before serving a file, and only the first match wins, so
# specific rules go above wildcards. The .html twins are here because Pages
# only rewrites .html to its clean URL after this table has had its say.

# --- Renames -----------------------------------------------------------
# "Edge and Console Routing" -> "The Public Path Table" (#1339)
/edge-and-console-routing              /public-path-table                301
/edge-and-console-routing.html         /public-path-table                301
/zh_CN/edge-and-console-routing        /zh_CN/public-path-table          301
/zh_CN/edge-and-console-routing.html   /zh_CN/public-path-table          301

